    isbefore: []  # 6385
    duplicate_of: []  # 6385
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 6385
    pr_ref:  # 6385
    description: "W1 of ADR-0056. Independently valuable; fires on the current tree.\n\n`catalog.validate_pass_dependencies` has 11 call sites, all in tests, zero in\nproduction — LIVE.md §1.7's instrument-with-no-reader defect. INV-hujog asks for\nit to be wired as a GATE. Do not: raising is the withholding direction\n(LIVE.md §2), and a gate aborts the whole survey on any repo whose declarations\nare stale — and the ~69 `depends_on` conjuncts across ~28 linkers have NEVER\nbeen enforced, so some are stale, over-broad or missing.\n\nINSTEAD, wire the same predicate as a FALSIFICATION DETECTOR:\n\n  find_falsified_dependencies(active_passes, runs) -> list[(pass_id, clauses)]\n\nreporting passes that EMITTED OUTPUT despite an unsatisfied conjunct. Such a\npass proves its own declaration wrong. Keep `validate_pass_dependencies`\nunchanged so its 11 tests stay green (LIVE.md §1.6: re-point, don't strike).\nFalsification never suppresses anything, so it cannot lose an edge.\n\nWHAT IT BUYS: the declaration set gets its first real audit. Open questions it\nwould settle, none of which anyone has had to answer: `method_call_recovery.py`\ncontains zero occurrences of `go` while `method-call-recovery-linker` omits `go`\nfrom a 12-language clause — correct declaration, or coverage gap? Same shape for\n`inheritance-linker` (omits go/cpp) and `build-target-linker` ([[\"toml\",\"json\"]]).\n\nSIZING NOTE, verified: on the CURRENT self-survey this reports ZERO hits. The\nanalysis behind ADR-0056 cited `database-query-linker` falsifying [[\"sql\"], ...]\nwhile reading 353 files, but that rests on a Sep-15 cached artifact; the repo has\nsince gained a .sql file and the clause is now satisfied. The MECHANISM is real\n(any repo without SQL files reproduces it) — but do not expect a hit on\nhypergumbo itself, and do not treat an empty result here as the detector failing.\nRun it across a polyglot corpus.\n\nDELIVERABLE: the predicate + a reader (a scripts/ entry or an advisory\nvalidation_report row) + tests. No production behaviour change."  # 6385
    fields: {}  # 6385
- op: discuss  # 26b4
  at: '2026-09-17T02:02:57Z'  # 26b4
  by: agent  # 26b4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 26b4
  clock: 2  # 26b4
  nonce: 26b4  # 26b4
  message: "IMPLEMENTED AND MEASURED. The detector fires; the declaration set has now had its first real audit and it FAILS.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED\n  catalog.find_falsified_dependencies(passes, runs) -- the CNF predicate re-pointed from gate to detector.\n  catalog.format_falsified_dependencies / emit_falsified_dependency_summary -- the reader, wired in cli.py next to emit_silence_summary, one stderr line, silent when clean.\n  validate_pass_dependencies untouched; its 11 tests stay green (re-point, don't strike).\n\nONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION FROM THIS ROW'S SIGNATURE. It is find_falsified_dependencies(passes, runs), not (active_passes, runs). The active set is DERIVED from runs -- the ground truth of what actually ran -- which is the whole difference between a forecast and a measurement. Passing an active set in would have made it a second validator.\n\nTHE AUDIT. 893 surveys on disk carrying analysis_runs; 261 (29.2%) have at least one falsified declaration; 6 distinct (pass, clause) across 5 passes. Full table on the new row WI-rasal, which carries the repair.\n\nTHE SIZING NOTE IN THIS ROW IS SUPERSEDED, and in the direction that matters. It said \"on the CURRENT self-survey this reports ZERO hits ... do not expect a hit on hypergumbo itself\". True, and I confirmed it -- the self-survey at tip emits no advisory line. But \"run it across a polyglot corpus\" undersold it: a survey of compose-go (Go-only, 150 files) at tip fires immediately, naming inheritance-linker and type-hierarchy-linker. The database-query-linker instance this row calls stale is stale only on THIS repo; across the corpus it is the second most common hit, 67 surveys.\n\nTHIS ROW'S THREE OPEN QUESTIONS ARE ANSWERED, all the same way: coverage gap, not correct declaration. Hand-verified on logrus (47 .go files) -- inheritance-linker emitted 30 EDGES while NONE of its twelve declared languages ran. The edges are real. The declaration is wrong.\n\nADR-0056's ORDERING CONSEQUENCE, since this row is W1 and it changes W2/W3. ADR-0056 §\"What would change this decision\" item 2: \"Ten hits means declaration repair, not W2, is the blocker.\" There are 6 distinct falsified declarations over 261 surveys. By the ADR's own criterion the blocker is declaration repair (WI-rasal), and I am recording that rather than quietly proceeding.\n\nTWO DEFECTS FOUND IN PASSING, both filed:\n  (1) The only live-tree check of the declaration set was A CONTROL THAT COULD NOT FAIL. TestCatalogStaticConsistency calls get_default_catalog() without importing the linker modules, which register by import side-effect -- so in isolation it validated 118 analyzers and ZERO depends_on conjuncts. Whether it checked 73 clauses or nothing depended on which other test module had imported cli first. Repaired here, with a mutation control proving it now goes red. Its sibling validate_pass_name_resolution has ZERO call sites anywhere despite a docstring claiming it \"runs at catalog-build time and in CI\".\n  (2) Pass.requires names the wrong distribution for 25 of 26 grammar-gated literals -> WI-pakof."  # 26b4
